# This repository stores text files with CRLF - exactly as they are in the
# working tree.
#
# Without this setting Git normalizes every touched text file to LF on commit as
# soon as core.autocrlf=true is set (the usual case on Windows). Because the
# stored files carry CRLF, the whole file then counts as changed instead of only
# the lines that really changed - and every review becomes useless.
#
# -text turns this conversion off: Git stores the bytes as they are.
* -text
